    "subject": "Physics",
    "questionEn": "A satellite of mass M 2 is revolving around earth in a circular orbit at a height of R 3 from earth surface. The angular momentum of the satellite is M √ GMR x . The value of x is _________ , where M and R are the mass and radius of earth, respectively. ( G is the gravitational constant)",
