    "explanationEn": "Let the first term of the A.P. be a and common difference be d . Then, from the question: first term of the G.P. = d common ratio of the G.P. = a Now use the given conditions one by one. 1. Sum of first 10 terms of the A.P. We know, S 10 = 10 2 [ 2 a + ( 10 − 1 ) d ] So, 160 = 5 ( 2 a + 9 d ) 2 a + 9 d = 32 . . . ( 1 ) 2. Sum of first 2 terms of the G.P. The G.P. has first term d and common ratio a . So its first two terms are: d , d a Their sum is 8 : d + d a = 8 d ( 1 + a ) = 8 . . . ( 2 ) 3. Express d from equation (1) From 2 a + 9 d = 32 we get 9 d = 32 − 2 a d = 32 − 2 a 9 Substitute this in equation (2): 32 − 2 a 9 ( 1 + a ) = 8 Multiply by 9 : ( 32 − 2 a ) ( 1 + a ) = 72 Expand: 32 + 32 a − 2 a − 2 a 2 = 72 32 + 30 a − 2 a 2 = 72 − 2 a 2 + 30 a − 40 = 0 Divide by − 2 : a 2 − 15 a + 20 = 0 4. Find values of a Using quadratic formula: a = 15 ± √ 225 − 80 2 a = 15 ± √ 145 2 Now we need the possible values of the first term of the G.P., which is d . 5. Find corresponding values of d From equation (1): d = 32 − 2 a 9 For the two values of a , the two values of d are obtained. But the question asks for the sum of all possible values of the first term of the G.P. , i.e. sum of both possible values of d . Let the two roots of the quadratic in a be a 1 and a 2 . Then corresponding values of d are d 1 = 32 − 2 a 1 9 , d 2 = 32 − 2 a 2 9 So, d 1 + d 2 = 32 − 2 a 1 9 + 32 − 2 a 2 9 d 1 + d 2 = 64 − 2 ( a 1 + a 2 ) 9 For the quadratic a 2 − 15 a + 20 = 0 sum of roots is a 1 + a 2 = 15 Hence, d 1 + d 2 = 64 − 2 ( 15 ) 9 d 1 + d 2 = 64 − 30 9 = 34 9 Therefore, the required sum is 34 9 So the correct option is A .",
