    "explanationEn": "Let I = ∫ π 4 − π 4 32 cos 4 ⁡ x 1 + e sin ⁡ x d x We will use the standard property: If I = ∫ a − a f ( x ) d x , then I = ∫ a − a f ( − x ) d x and hence 2 I = ∫ a − a ( f ( x ) + f ( − x ) ) d x Now here, f ( x ) = 32 cos 4 ⁡ x 1 + e sin ⁡ x So, f ( − x ) = 32 cos 4 ⁡ ( − x ) 1 + e sin ⁡ ( − x ) Using cos ⁡ ( − x ) = cos ⁡ x and sin ⁡ ( − x ) = − sin ⁡ x , f ( − x ) = 32 cos 4 ⁡ x 1 + e − sin ⁡ x Therefore, f ( x ) + f ( − x ) = 32 cos 4 ⁡ x ( 1 1 + e sin ⁡ x + 1 1 + e − sin ⁡ x ) Now simplify the bracket: 1 1 + e sin ⁡ x + 1 1 + e − sin ⁡ x Let t = e sin ⁡ x . Then e − sin ⁡ x = 1 t . So, 1 1 + t + 1 1 + 1 t = 1 1 + t + t 1 + t = 1 Hence, f ( x ) + f ( − x ) = 32 cos 4 ⁡ x So, 2 I = ∫ π 4 − π 4 32 cos 4 ⁡ x d x Thus, I = 16 ∫ π 4 − π 4 cos 4 ⁡ x d x Since cos 4 ⁡ x is an even function, I = 32 ∫ π 4 0 cos 4 ⁡ x d x Now use the identity cos 4 ⁡ x = ( cos 2 ⁡ x ) 2 = ( 1 + cos ⁡ 2 x 2 ) 2 which gives cos 4 ⁡ x = 3 + 4 cos ⁡ 2 x + cos ⁡ 4 x 8 Therefore, I = 32 ∫ π 4 0 3 + 4 cos ⁡ 2 x + cos ⁡ 4 x 8 d x I = 4 ∫ π 4 0 ( 3 + 4 cos ⁡ 2 x + cos ⁡ 4 x ) d x Now integrate termwise: ∫ 3 d x = 3 x , ∫ 4 cos ⁡ 2 x d x = 2 sin ⁡ 2 x , ∫ cos ⁡ 4 x d x = sin ⁡ 4 x 4 So, I = 4 [ 3 x + 2 sin ⁡ 2 x + sin ⁡ 4 x 4 ] π 4 0 At x = π 4 , 3 x = 3 π 4 , sin ⁡ 2 x = sin ⁡ π 2 = 1 , sin ⁡ 4 x = sin ⁡ π = 0 At x = 0 , 3 x = 0 , sin ⁡ 0 = 0 Hence, I = 4 ( 3 π 4 + 2 ) I = 3 π + 8 So the correct answer is: 3 π + 8 Hence, Option B is correct.",
