    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "Enthalpy of atomisation is the energy needed to break 1 mole of a metal (in solid state) into its separate atoms (in gaseous state). In transition metals, metallic bonding becomes stronger when there are more unpaired electrons. This is because unpaired electrons can take part more effectively in metal–metal bonding. So, if a transition metal atom has a large number of unpaired electrons, its metallic bonds are stronger, and more energy is required to convert the metal into atoms. Therefore, more unpaired electrons ∝ stronger metallic bonding ∝ higher enthalpy of atomisation. Hence, Statement I is correct . [ Fe ( H 2 O ) 6 ] 3 + is an octahedral complex (coordination number 6 ). In an octahedral field, the d -orbitals split as: d x y = d x z = d y z d x 2 − y 2 = d z 2 [ Ni ( Cl ) 4 ] 2 − is a tetrahedral complex (coordination number 4 ). In a tetrahedral field, the splitting is reversed compared to octahedral, i.e.: d x 2 − y 2 = d z 2 d x y = d x z = d y z So, the given splittings match the correct orbital splitting patterns for these two geometries. Hence, Statement II is also correct .",
