    "questionEn": "One half cell in a voltaic cell is constructed by dipping silver rod in AgNO 3 solution of unknown concentration, other half cell is Zn rod dipped in 1 molar solution of ZnSO 4 . A voltage of 1.60 V is measured at 298 K for this cell. What is the concentration of Ag + ions used in terms of log ⁡ x ( x = [ Ag + ] ) ? E ⊖ Zn 2 + / Zn = − 0.76 V , E ⊖ Ag + / Ag = + 0.80 V , 2.303 RT F = 0.059 V",
