    "explanationEn": "When the block is at rest on the incline, the forces acting on it are : F g = mg is weight acting vertically downward. N = Normal force acting perpendicular to the incline. f s = Static friction acting up the incline, preventing the block from sliding down. Since the block is at rest relative to the incline, the frictional force must balance the component of gravity acting down the slope : f s = mg sin ⁡ θ The mass of block is m = 1 kg , acceleration due to gravity is g = 10 m / s 2 and θ = 30 ∘ So, value of static friction is f s = 1 × 10 × sin ⁡ 30 ∘ = 10 × 0.5 = 5 N The friction force is 5 N directed up along the incline. As the entire assembly moves vertically upward with a constant velocity v = 4 m / s , so in time t = 2 s , the vertical displacement S is: S = v × t = 4 × 2 = 8 m Work done is defined as W = F ⃗ ⋅ d ⃗ = F d cos ⁡ φ , where φ is the angle between the force and the displacement. The angle between the friction force and the vertical is 90 ∘ − 30 ∘ = 60 ∘ = φ . So, work done by frictional force is, W = f s × S × cos ⁡ 60 ∘ ⇒ W = 5 × 8 × 0.5 J ⇒ W = 5 × 4 = 20 J Therefore, the work done by the frictional force is 20 J . Hence, the correct option is (A).",
