    "explanationEn": "Internal energy ( U ) of an ideal gas depends only on temperature. The change in internal energy for any process is given by: Δ U = nC v Δ T = nC v ( T f − T i ) According to Mayer's relation, C p − C v = R . C p C v − 1 = R C v Since γ = C p C v , then γ − 1 = R C v ⇒ C v = R γ − 1 . Substituting C v back into the Δ U equation: Δ U = nR γ − 1 ( T f − T i ) Thus, Statement I is true. From the law of equipartition of energy, the molar specific heat at constant volume is C v = f 2 R , where f is the degree of freedom. Using C p = C v + R = f 2 R + R = R ( 1 + f 2 ) . The ratio γ = C p C v = R ( 1 + f 2 ) ( f / 2 ) R = 1 + f / 2 f / 2 = 2 f + 1 . So, γ = 1 + 2 f. Thus, Statement II is true. Statement II is the definition of γ in terms of degrees of freedom, but Statement I is based on Mayer's relation which is the definition of C v , i.e., not directly from the degrees of freedom. Therefore, both A and R are true but R is the correct explanation of A . Thus, the correct option is (B).",
