    "subject": "Chemistry",
    "questionEn": "An electrochemical cell consists of the following two redox couples, M x + ( aq ) / M ( s ) [ E Θ red = + 0.15 V ] and Fe 3 + ( aq ) / Fe ( s ) [ E Θ red = − 0.036 V ] . The cell EMF ( E cell ) is recorded to be 0.2057 V . If the reaction quotient of the electrochemical reaction is found to be 10 − 2 , then the value of x is _ _ _ _ .(Nearest integer) [Given : M is a p-block metal and 2.303 R T F = 0.059 V ]",
