    "explanationEn": "Since the right angle is at B = ( 4 , 8 ) , and A , C lie on the parabola y 2 = 16 x , we first parametrize the parabola in the standard NCERT form. For y 2 = 4 a x , we have 4 a = 16 ⇒ a = 4 . So any point on the parabola can be written as ( a t 2 , 2 a t ) = ( 4 t 2 , 8 t ) . Thus let A = ( 4 t 2 1 , 8 t 1 ) , C = ( 4 t 2 2 , 8 t 2 ) . Also, the point B = ( 4 , 8 ) lies on the parabola and corresponds to parameter t = 1 , since ( 4 ⋅ 1 2 , 8 ⋅ 1 ) = ( 4 , 8 ) . So B is the point with parameter 1 . Now, for the triangle A B C to be right-angled at B , the slopes of B A and B C must satisfy m B A m B C = − 1. For parabola y 2 = 4 a x , the slope of chord joining parameter points t 1 and t 2 is 2 a ( t 2 − t 1 ) a ( t 2 2 − t 2 1 ) = 2 t 1 + t 2 . So slope of chord joining parameter 1 and t 1 is m B A = 2 1 + t 1 , and slope of chord joining parameter 1 and t 2 is m B C = 2 1 + t 2 . Since these are perpendicular, 2 1 + t 1 ⋅ 2 1 + t 2 = − 1. Hence 4 ( 1 + t 1 ) ( 1 + t 2 ) = − 1 which gives ( 1 + t 1 ) ( 1 + t 2 ) = − 4. So, t 1 t 2 + t 1 + t 2 + 1 = − 4 or t 1 t 2 + t 1 + t 2 = − 5. Now let the centroid of △ A B C be G ( h , k ) . Using centroid formula, h = 4 t 2 1 + 4 + 4 t 2 2 3 = 4 3 ( t 2 1 + t 2 2 + 1 ) , k = 8 t 1 + 8 + 8 t 2 3 = 8 3 ( t 1 + t 2 + 1 ) . Let S = t 1 + t 2 , P = t 1 t 2 . Then from the perpendicularity condition, P + S = − 5. Also, t 2 1 + t 2 2 = S 2 − 2 P . So h = 4 3 ( S 2 − 2 P + 1 ) . Since P = − 5 − S , h = 4 3 ( S 2 − 2 ( − 5 − S ) + 1 ) h = 4 3 ( S 2 + 2 S + 11 ) . Also, k = 8 3 ( S + 1 ) . From this, S + 1 = 3 k 8 ⇒ S = 3 k 8 − 1. Substitute into h : h = 4 3 [ ( 3 k 8 − 1 ) 2 + 2 ( 3 k 8 − 1 ) + 11 ] . Now simplify: ( 3 k 8 − 1 ) 2 = 9 k 2 64 − 3 k 4 + 1 and 2 ( 3 k 8 − 1 ) = 3 k 4 − 2. So inside the bracket, 9 k 2 64 − 3 k 4 + 1 + 3 k 4 − 2 + 11 = 9 k 2 64 + 10. Hence h = 4 3 ( 9 k 2 64 + 10 ) = 3 k 2 16 + 40 3 . Therefore, h − 40 3 = 3 k 2 16 . Rearranging, k 2 = 16 3 ( h − 40 3 ) . So the locus is a parabola: k 2 = 4 a ( h − 40 3 ) with 4 a = 16 3 ⇒ a = 4 3 . Length of latus rectum of this parabola is 4 a = 16 3 . Therefore, three times the length of latus rectum is 3 × 16 3 = 16. So the required answer is 16 .",
