    "explanationEn": "We need the area of the region { ( x , y ) : y ≤ π − | x | , y ≤ | x sin ⁡ x | , y ≥ 0 } . This means the required area is the area under the curve y = min ( π − | x | , | x sin ⁡ x | ) and above the x -axis. So the area is A = ∫ min ( π − | x | , | x sin ⁡ x | ) d x over the values of x where the region exists. Since y ≥ 0 and y ≤ π − | x | , we must have π − | x | ≥ 0 ⟹ | x | ≤ π . Hence the region lies in [ − π , π ] . Also, both functions π − | x | and | x sin ⁡ x | are even functions, so the region is symmetric about the y -axis. Therefore, A = 2 ∫ π 0 min ( π − x , x sin ⁡ x ) d x . Now for 0 ≤ x ≤ π , we have sin ⁡ x ≥ 0 , so | x sin ⁡ x | = x sin ⁡ x . Thus, A = 2 ∫ π 0 min ( π − x , x sin ⁡ x ) d x . Now compare π − x and x sin ⁡ x on [ 0 , π ] . At x = 0 , π − x = π , x sin ⁡ x = 0. At x = π , π − x = 0 , x sin ⁡ x = 0. Check where they meet: x sin ⁡ x = π − x . It is easy to see that x = π 2 satisfies this, because π 2 sin ⁡ π 2 = π 2 = π − π 2 . Also, on [ 0 , π / 2 ] , we have x sin ⁡ x ≤ π − x , and on [ π / 2 , π ] , we have π − x ≤ x sin ⁡ x . So, A = 2 [ ∫ π / 2 0 x sin ⁡ x d x + ∫ π π / 2 ( π − x ) d x ] . Now evaluate each integral. First, ∫ x sin ⁡ x d x = − x cos ⁡ x + ∫ cos ⁡ x d x = − x cos ⁡ x + sin ⁡ x . Therefore, ∫ π / 2 0 x sin ⁡ x d x = [ − x cos ⁡ x + sin ⁡ x ] π / 2 0 = 1. Next, ∫ π π / 2 ( π − x ) d x . Let u = π − x . Then as x goes from π / 2 to π , u goes from π / 2 to 0 . Or directly, ∫ π π / 2 ( π − x ) d x = [ π x − x 2 2 ] π π / 2 . Compute: At x = π , π 2 − π 2 2 = π 2 2 . At x = π 2 , π ⋅ π 2 − 1 2 ( π 2 ) 2 = π 2 2 − π 2 8 = 3 π 2 8 . So, ∫ π π / 2 ( π − x ) d x = π 2 2 − 3 π 2 8 = π 2 8 . Hence, A = 2 ( 1 + π 2 8 ) = 2 + π 2 4 . Therefore, the correct answer is 2 + π 2 4 So, Option B is correct.",
