    "explanationEn": "Let the degree of the real polynomial f be n . Since f ( x ) = f ′ ( x ) f ′ ′ ( x ) for all x , we compare degrees: deg ⁡ ( f ) = deg ⁡ ( f ′ ) + deg ⁡ ( f ′ ′ ) n = ( n − 1 ) + ( n − 2 ) = 2 n − 3 ⇒ n = 3 So f must be a cubic polynomial. Write f ( x ) = a x 3 + b x 2 + c x + d Given f ( 0 ) = 0 , we get d = 0 . Hence f ( x ) = a x 3 + b x 2 + c x Now find derivatives: f ′ ( x ) = 3 a x 2 + 2 b x + c f ′ ′ ( x ) = 6 a x + 2 b Use the given condition f ( x ) = f ′ ( x ) f ′ ′ ( x ) : ( a x 3 + b x 2 + c x ) = ( 3 a x 2 + 2 b x + c ) ( 6 a x + 2 b ) Now compare coefficients of like powers of x . For x 3 : a = 18 a 2 ⇒ a = 1 18 ( since a ≠ 0 for a cubic ) For x 2 : b = 6 a b + 12 a b b = 18 a b With a = 1 18 , this becomes b = b , so it gives no new condition on b . For x : c = 4 b 2 + 6 a c c = 4 b 2 + c 3 ( ∵ 6 a = 1 3 ) ⇒ 2 c 3 = 4 b 2 ⇒ c = 6 b 2 For the constant term: 0 = 2 b c ⇒ b c = 0 But c = 6 b 2 , so b c = b ( 6 b 2 ) = 6 b 3 = 0 ⇒ b = 0 , and then c = 0 . So the polynomial is f ( x ) = 1 18 x 3 Now compute the required value: f ′ ( x ) = 1 6 x 2 ⇒ f ′ ( 2 ) = 1 6 ⋅ 4 = 2 3 f ′ ′ ( x ) = 1 3 x ⇒ f ′ ′ ( 2 ) = 1 3 ⋅ 2 = 2 3 ∫ 2 0 f ( x ) d x = ∫ 2 0 1 18 x 3 d x = 1 18 [ x 4 4 ] 2 0 = 1 18 ⋅ 16 4 = 2 9 Add them: f ′ ( 2 ) + f ′ ′ ( 2 ) + ∫ 2 0 f ( x ) d x = 2 3 + 2 3 + 2 9 = 14 9 Finally, 36 ( f ′ ( 2 ) + f ′ ′ ( 2 ) + ∫ 2 0 f ( x ) d x ) = 36 ⋅ 14 9 = 56",
