    "explanationEn": "Let K = sin ⁡ ( π 18 ) sin ⁡ ( 5 π 18 ) sin ⁡ ( 7 π 18 ) We need to find sin ⁡ ( 10 K π 3 ) First, write the angles in degrees: π 18 = 10 ∘ , 5 π 18 = 50 ∘ , 7 π 18 = 70 ∘ So, K = sin ⁡ 10 ∘ sin ⁡ 50 ∘ sin ⁡ 70 ∘ Now use the standard identity: sin ⁡ 3 x = 4 sin ⁡ x sin ⁡ ( 60 ∘ + x ) sin ⁡ ( 60 ∘ − x ) Taking x = 10 ∘ , sin ⁡ 30 ∘ = 4 sin ⁡ 10 ∘ sin ⁡ 70 ∘ sin ⁡ 50 ∘ Since sin ⁡ 30 ∘ = 1 2 we get 1 2 = 4 sin ⁡ 10 ∘ sin ⁡ 50 ∘ sin ⁡ 70 ∘ Hence, sin ⁡ 10 ∘ sin ⁡ 50 ∘ sin ⁡ 70 ∘ = 1 8 Therefore, K = 1 8 Now substitute in the required expression: sin ⁡ ( 10 K π 3 ) = sin ⁡ ( 10 3 ⋅ 1 8 π ) = sin ⁡ ( 10 π 24 ) = sin ⁡ ( 5 π 12 ) Now, 5 π 12 = 75 ∘ So, sin ⁡ 75 ∘ = sin ⁡ ( 45 ∘ + 30 ∘ ) Using the formula sin ⁡ ( A + B ) : sin ⁡ 75 ∘ = sin ⁡ 45 ∘ cos ⁡ 30 ∘ + cos ⁡ 45 ∘ sin ⁡ 30 ∘ = 1 √ 2 ⋅ √ 3 2 + 1 √ 2 ⋅ 1 2 = √ 3 + 1 2 √ 2 So the value is √ 3 + 1 2 √ 2 Hence, the correct option is A.",
