    "explanationEn": "x + 2 y + z = 5 2 x + y + α z = 5 8 x + 4 y + β z = 18 For a system of three linear equations to have no solution , it is necessary that the coefficient matrix be singular , i.e. its determinant is zero: Δ = 0 . Δ = ∣ 1 2 1 2 1 α 8 4 β ∣ = 0 Δ = 1 ( β − 4 α ) − 2 ( 2 β − 8 α ) + 1 ( 0 ) = 0 = β − 4 α − 4 β + 16 α = 0 ⇒ 4 α = β Now substitute β = 4 α in the third equation. Then the left side of the third equation becomes 8 x + 4 y + 4 α z , which is exactly 4 times the left side of the second equation 2 x + y + α z . But the constants do not match: 4 × 5 = 20 , whereas the third equation has 18 . So we get 4 × ( 2 x + y + α z ) = 20 but 8 x + 4 y + 4 α z = 18 , which is a contradiction. Hence, the system is inconsistent and has no solution . Therefore, β α = 4 α α = 4 .",
