    "explanationEn": "The expected value of a discrete random variable is given by the formula : E ( X ) = ∑ X i ⋅ P ( X i ) Using the data from the table : E ( X ) = ( 4 k ⋅ 2 15 ) + ( 30 k 7 ⋅ 1 15 ) + ( 32 k 7 ⋅ 2 15 ) + ( 34 k 7 ⋅ 1 5 ) + ( 36 k 7 ⋅ 1 15 ) + ( 38 k 7 ⋅ 2 15 ) + ( 40 k 7 ⋅ 1 5 ) + ( 6 k ⋅ 1 15 ) Take k 15 factor common E ( X ) = k 15 [ 8 + 30 7 + 64 7 + 102 7 + 36 7 + 76 7 + 120 7 + 6 ] E ( X ) = k 15 [ 14 + 30 + 64 + 102 + 36 + 76 + 120 7 ] E ( X ) = k 15 [ 14 + 428 7 ] E ( X ) = k 15 [ 98 + 428 7 ] = k 15 ⋅ 526 7 = 526 k 105 Given that E ( X ) = 263 15 : 263 15 = 526 k 105 263 = 526 k 7 k = 263 × 7 526 = 1 × 7 2 = 7 2 = 3.5 Identify X values where X 20 Substitute k = 7 2 into each X : X 1 = 4 × 7 2 = 14 ( 20 ) X 4 = 34 7 × 7 2 = 17 ( 20 ) X 2 = 30 7 × 7 2 = 15 ( 20 ) X 5 = 36 7 × 7 2 = 18 ( 20 ) X 3 = 32 7 × 7 2 = 16 ( 20 ) X 6 = 38 7 × 7 2 = 19 ( 20 ) X 7 = 40 7 × 7 2 = 20 ( Not 20 ) X 8 = 6 × 7 2 = 21 ( Not 20 ) Calculate P ( X 20 ) : Sum the probabilities for X = 14 , 15 , 16 , 17 , 18 , and 19: P ( X 20 ) = P ( X = 14 ) + P ( X = 15 ) + P ( X = 16 ) + P ( X = 17 ) + P ( X = 18 ) + P ( X = 19 ) ⇒ P ( X 20 ) = 2 15 + 1 15 + 2 15 + 3 15 + 1 15 + 2 15 ⇒ P ( X 20 ) = 11 15",
