    "questionEn": "A brass wire of length 2 m and radius 1 mm at 27 ∘ C is held taut between two rigid supports. Initially it was cooled to a temperature of − 43 ∘ C creating a tension T in the wire. The temperature to which the wire has to be cooled in order to increase the tension in it to 1.4 T , is _ _ _ _ ∘ C .",
