    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "Initially, the block is floating. The weight of the block is balanced by the buoyant force ( F B ) . Let h be the height of the submerged part of the block. Mg = F B = V submerged × ρ liquid × g ⇒ Mg = ( A × h ) ρ g When the block is depressed by a small distance x downwards, the volume of the displaced liquid increases by A ⋅ x . This creates an extra buoyant force which acts as the restoring force. The additional buoyant force is : F restoring = − ( Additional Volume ) × ρ × g F restoring = − ( Ax ) ρ g Since the force is proportional to displacement x and acts opposite to it ( F ∝ − x ), the motion is Simple Harmonic Motion (SHM). Using Newton's Second Law ( F = Ma ) : Ma = − ( ρ Ag ) x ⇒ a = − ( ρ A g M ) x . Standard equation for SHM acceleration is a = − ω 2 x Comparing the two equations: ω 2 = ρ Ag M ⇒ ω = √ ρ Ag M The time period T is given by T = 2 π ω . ⇒ T = 2 π √ M ρ Ag Hence, the correct option is (C).",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "tags": [
      "Physics",
      "JEE Main 2026",
      "January Session"
    ]
