    "explanationEn": "The spring constant k of a spring is inversely proportional to the length L of the spring. k ∝ 1 L This means that the product of the spring constant and the length is a constant for a given spring: k ⋅ L = Constant The force constant of original spring is k o = 15 N / m . Let the original length be L . The spring is cut into two pieces with a length ratio of 1 : 3 . x + 3 x = L ⇒ x = L 4 Hence, the length of smaller spring is L 1 = x = L 4 and the length of larger spring is L 2 = 3 x = 3 L 4 . Let k 1 be the force constant of the smaller piece. Using the inverse proportionality relationship: k o L o = k 1 L 1 ⇒ 15 × L = k 1 × ( L 4 ) ⇒ k 1 = 60 N / m Therefore, the force constant of smaller piece is 60 N / m . Hence, the correct option is (C).",
