    "explanationEn": "When a mass m is suspended from a spring of constant k , the spring stretches. If the stretch in spring is x , kx = mg ⇒ x = mg k The potential energy ( U ) stored in the spring is given by : U = 1 2 kx 2 Substituting x = mg k : U = 1 2 k ( mg k ) 2 = ( mg ) 2 2 k Mass of block A is m A = 100 g . The spring constant is k A . So, the stored energy in spring A is E A = E . Using the formula : E = ( m A g ) 2 2 k A Mass of block B is m B = 200 g = 2 × 100 g = 2 m A The spring constant of spring B is k B . It is given that 4 k A = 3 k B ⇒ k B = 4 3 k A . So, the stored energy in spring B is E B = ( m B g ) 2 2 k B Substituting m B = 2 m A and k B = 4 3 k A : E B = ( 2 m A g ) 2 2 ( 4 3 k A ) ⇒ E B = 4 × 3 8 × ( m A g ) 2 k A ⇒ E B = 12 8 × ( m A g ) 2 k A ⇒ E B = 3 2 × ( m A g ) 2 k A ⇒ E B = 3 × ( ( m A g ) 2 2 k A ) ⇒ E B = 3 E",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
