    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "Before Collision : The masses of the spheres are, m A = 15 kg , m B = 25 kg The initial velocities of the spheres are, u A = 10 m / s , u B = − 30 m / s Hence, the kinetic energy of system before collision is, K i = 1 2 m A u 2 A + 1 2 m B u 2 B ⇒ K i = 1 2 ( 15 ) ( 10 ) 2 + 1 2 ( 25 ) ( 30 ) 2 = 750 + 11250 = 12000 J Since the collision is perfectly inelastic, the spheres stick together and move with a common final velocity v f . Using conservation of linear momentum, m A u A + m B u B = ( m A + m B ) v f ⇒ ( 15 ) ( 10 ) + ( 25 ) ( − 30 ) = ( 15 + 25 ) v f ⇒ 150 − 750 = 40 v f − 600 = 40 v f ⇒ v f = − 15 m / s (The negative sign indicates the combined mass moves in the direction of the 25 kg sphere.) So, the final kinetic energy of the system is K f = 1 2 ( m A + m B ) v 2 f ⇒ K f = 1 2 ( 40 ) ( 15 ) 2 ⇒ K f = 4500 J The loss in kinetic energy appears as heat (Q). Q = K i − K f ⇒ Q = 12000 J − 4500 J Q = 7500 J Using the heat capacity formula Q = mc ⁡ Δ T . Where, total mass (m) of the spheres is 40 kg , the specific heat (c) of the material of spheres is 31 cal / kg ⋅ ∘ C . As 1 cal = 4.2 J , so c = 31 × 4.2 J / kg ⋅ ∘ C = 130.2 J / kg ⋅ ∘ C Substituting the values in heat capacity formula, 7500 = 40 × 130.2 × Δ T ⇒ 7500 = 5208 × Δ T ⇒ Δ T = 7500 5208 ≈ 1.44 ∘ C Therefore, the rise in temperature is 1.44 ∘ C . Hence, the correct option is (B).",
