    "subject": "Physics",
    "questionEn": "Given below are two statements : Statement I : A satellite is moving around earth in the orbit very close to the earth surface. The time period of revolution of satellite depends upon the density of earth. Statement II : The time period of revolution of the satellite is T = 2 π √ R e g (for satellite very close to the earth surface), where R e radius of earth and g acceleration due to gravity. In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below :",
