    "explanationEn": "The mass of the rod is M = 20 m The length of the rod is L = 12 cm Distance of mass m from center, r 1 = 4 cm Distance of mass 2 m from center, r 2 = 2 cm Let the geometrical center of the rod be the origin ( 0 , 0 ) . The position of the new center of mass ( x cm ) after the collision : x cm = M ( 0 ) + m ( r 1 ) − 2 m ( r 2 ) M + m + 2 m ⇒ x cm = 20 m ( 0 ) + m ( 4 ) − 2 m ( 2 ) 23 m ⇒ x cm = 4 m − 4 m 23 m = 0 Since x cm = 0 , the center of mass of the system does not shift. The entire system will only rotate about the geometrical center of the rod. The initial angular momentum ( L i ) of the system about the center must equal the final angular momentum ( L f ) . The initial angular momentum of the system is, L i = ( m ⋅ v ⋅ r 1 ) + ( 2 m ⋅ v ⋅ r 2 ) ⇒ L i = m ⋅ v ⋅ 4 + 2 m ⋅ v ⋅ 2 ⇒ L i = 4 mv + 4 mv = 8 mv The final moment of inertia ( I f ) about the center is the sum of the moment of inertia of the rod and the two point masses. I f = I rod + I m + I 2 m ⇒ I f = M L 2 12 + m r 2 1 + 2 m r 2 2 ⇒ I f = ( 20 m ) ( 12 ) 2 12 + m ( 4 ) 2 + 2 m ( 2 ) 2 ⇒ I f = 20 m ( 12 ) + 16 m + 2 m ( 4 ) = 264 m The angular momentum of the system is given as L = I ω , where ω is the angular speed and I is the moment of inertia. Using conservation of angular momentum, L i = L f ⇒ 8 mv = 264 m ω ⇒ ω = 8 mv 264 m ⇒ ω v = 1 33 ⇒ v ω = 33",
