    "questionEn": "A conducting circular loop of area 1.0 m 2 is placed perpendicular to a magnetic field which varies as B = sin ⁡ ( 100 t ) Tesla. If the resistance of the loop is 100 Ω , then the average thermal energy dissipated in the loop in one period is _ _ _ _ J.",
