    "questionEn": "The standard reduction potentials at 298 K for the following half cells are given below : Cr 2 O 2 − 7 + 14 H + + 6 e − → 2 Cr 3 + + 7 H 2 O , E ∘ = 1.33 V Fe 3 + ( aq ) + 3 e − → Fe E ∘ = − 0.04 V Ni 2 + ( aq ) + 2 e − → Ni E ∘ = − 0.25 V Ag + ( aq ) + e − → Ag E ∘ = 0.80 V Au 3 + ( aq ) + 3 e − → Au E ∘ = 1.40 V Consider the given electrochemical reactions, The number of metal(s) which will be oxidized by Cr 2 O 2 − 7 , in aqueous solution is _________.",
