    "explanationEn": "For a particle performing simple harmonic motion (SHM), the maximum velocity v m a x can be calculated using the formula: v m a x = A ω where A is the amplitude of the motion and ω is the angular frequency. The angular frequency ω is related to the time period T by the formula: ω = 2 π T Given: Amplitude, A = 0.06 m Time period, T = 3.14 s First, we find the angular frequency: ω = 2 π T = 2 π 3.14 Substituting ω and A in the formula for v m a x : v m a x = A ω = 0.06 × 2 π 3.14 v m a x = 0.06 × 2 × 3.14 3.14 v m a x = 0.06 × 2 v m a x = 0.12 m / s To convert meters per second to centimeters per second, we use the conversion factor 1 m / s = 100 cm / s . Therefore, v m a x = 0.12 m / s × 100 cm / m = 12 cm / s Thus, the maximum velocity of the particle is 12 cm / s .",
