    "subject": "Physics",
    "questionEn": "Wheatstone bridge principle is used to measure the specific resistance ( S 1 ) of given wire, having length L , radius r . If X is the resistance of wire, then specific resistance is ; S 1 = X ( π r 2 L ) . If the length of the wire gets doubled then the value of specific resistance will be :",
