    "questionEn": "For a reversible reaction A ⇌ B , the Δ H forward reaction = 20 kJ mol − 1 . The activation energy of the uncatalysed forward reaction is 300 kJ mol − 1 . When the reaction is catalysed keeping the reactant concentration same, the rate of the catalysed forward reaction at 27 ∘ C is found to be same as that of the uncatalysed reaction at 327 ∘ C . The activation energy of the catalysed backward reaction is ___________ kJ mol − 1 .",
