    "explanationEn": "Let X be the number rolled on the die, and let W be the event that all balls drawn are white. We want to find the probability P ( W ) , which can be calculated using the law of total probability as follows : P ( W ) = ∑ x = 1 6 P ( W | X = x ) P ( X = x ) The probability of rolling any number from 1 to 6 on the die is equal, so P ( X = x ) = 1 6 for all x ∈ { 1 , 2 , 3 , 4 , 5 , 6 } . Now let's calculate the conditional probabilities P ( W | X = x ) for each possible value of x : 1. P ( W | X = 1 ) = 6 C 1 10 C 1 = 6 10 = 3 5 , since there are 6 white balls out of a total of 10 balls. 2. P ( W | X = 2 ) = 6 C 2 10 C 2 = 15 45 = 1 3 , since there are 15 ways to choose 2 white balls out of 6, and 45 ways to choose 2 balls out of 10. 3. P ( W | X = 3 ) = 6 C 3 10 C 3 = 20 120 = 1 6 , since there are 20 ways to choose 3 white balls out of 6, and 120 ways to choose 3 balls out of 10. 4. P ( W | X = 4 ) = 6 C 4 10 C 4 = 15 210 = 1 14 , since there are 15 ways to choose 4 white balls out of 6, and 210 ways to choose 4 balls out of 10. 5. P ( W | X = 5 ) = 6 C 5 10 C 5 = 6 252 = 1 42 , since there are 6 ways to choose 5 white balls out of 6, and 252 ways to choose 5 balls out of 10. 6. P ( W | X = 6 ) = 6 C 6 10 C 6 = 1 210 , since there are 1 ways to choose 6 white balls out of 6, and 210 ways to choose 6 balls out of 10. Using the law of total probability, we have : P ( W ) = 1 6 ( P ( W | X = 1 ) + P ( W | X = 2 ) + P ( W | X = 3 ) + P ( W | X = 4 ) + P ( W | X = 5 ) + P ( W | X = 6 ) ) P ( W ) = 1 6 ( 3 5 + 1 3 + 1 6 + 1 14 + 1 42 + 1 210 ) To simplify this expression, find a common denominator : P ( W ) = 1 6 ( 126 210 + 70 210 + 35 210 + 15 210 + 5 210 + 1 210 ) Add the fractions : P ( W ) = 1 6 ( 126 + 70 + 35 + 15 + 5 + 1 210 ) = 42 210 = 1 5",
