    "explanationEn": "Given equation is sin − 1 ⁡ ( x + 1 √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 ) − sin − 1 ⁡ ( x √ x 2 + 1 ) = π 4 . Let's denote: A = sin − 1 ⁡ ( x + 1 √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 ) , B = sin − 1 ⁡ ( x √ x 2 + 1 ) . So, we have the equation A − B = π 4 . We can also write this as A = B + π 4 . This gives us sin ⁡ ( A ) = sin ⁡ ( B + π 4 ) . We can use the identity sin ⁡ ( a + b ) = sin ⁡ a cos ⁡ b + cos ⁡ a sin ⁡ b and rewrite this equation as: x + 1 √ ( x + 1 ) 2 + 1 = x √ x 2 + 1 cos ⁡ ( π 4 ) + √ 1 − ( x √ x 2 + 1 ) 2 sin ⁡ ( π 4 ) . After simplifying, we get: x + 1 √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 √ 2 ( x √ x 2 + 1 + √ 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 ) . Let's square both sides to remove the square roots: On the left side, squaring gives: ( x + 1 √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 ) 2 = ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 . On the right side, squaring gives: ( 1 √ 2 ( x √ x 2 + 1 + √ 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 ) ) 2 = 1 2 ( x 2 x 2 + 1 + 2 x √ x 2 + 1 √ 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 + 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 ) . ∴ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( x 2 x 2 + 1 + 2 x √ x 2 + 1 √ 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 + 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 ) ⇒ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( 2 × x √ x 2 + 1 √ x 2 + 1 − x 2 x 2 + 1 + 1 ) ⇒ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( 2 × x √ x 2 + 1 1 √ x 2 + 1 + 1 ) ⇒ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( 2 × x x 2 + 1 + 1 ) ⇒ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( 2 x + x 2 + 1 x 2 + 1 ) ⇒ ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 2 x + 2 = 1 2 ( ( x + 1 ) 2 x 2 + 1 ) ⇒ x + 1 √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 = x + 1 √ 2 √ x 2 + 1 ⇒ x = − 1 OR √ x 2 + 2 x + 2 = √ 2 ⋅ √ x 2 + 1 ⇒ x = 0 , x = 2 (Rejected) S = { 0 , − 1 } ∑ x ∈ S ( sin ⁡ ( ( x 2 + x + 5 ) π 2 ) − cos ⁡ ( ( x 2 + x + 5 ) π ) ) = [ sin ⁡ ( 5 π 2 ) − cos ⁡ ( 5 π ) ] + [ sin ⁡ ( 5 π 2 ) − cos ⁡ ( 5 π ) ] = ( 1 − ( − 1 ) ) + ( 1 − ( − 1 ) ) = 2 + 2 = 4",
