    "subject": "Mathematics",
    "questionEn": "Let P ( 2 √ 3 √ 7 , 6 √ 7 ) , Q , R and S be four points on the ellipse 9 x 2 + 4 y 2 = 36 . Let PQ and RS be mutually perpendicular and pass through the origin. If 1 ( P Q ) 2 + 1 ( R S ) 2 = p q , where p and q are coprime, then p + q is equal to :",
