    "shift": 1,
    "subject": "Mathematics",
    "questionEn": "Let sets A and B have 5 elements each. Let the mean of the elements in sets A and B be 5 and 8 respectively and the variance of the elements in sets A and B be 12 and 20 respectively. A new set C of 10 elements is formed by subtracting 3 from each element of A and adding 2 to each element of B . Then the sum of the mean and variance of the elements of C is ___________.",
    "optionsEn": [
      "36",
      "40",
      "38",
      "32"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 2,
    "explanationEn": "To solve this problem, let's break it down step by step : Step 1 : Determine the mean of set C The mean of set A = 5 The mean of set B = 8 After subtracting 3 from each element in set A, the new mean becomes 5 − 3 = 2 . After adding 2 to each element in set B, the new mean becomes 8 + 2 = 10 . When we combine both modified sets to form set C, the mean of set C is the weighted average of the means of these modified sets: Mean of C = 5 × 2 + 5 × 10 10 = 10 + 50 10 = 6 Step 2 : Determine the variance of set C Variance is defined as the expectation of the squared deviation of a random variable from its mean. One property of variance is that, if you add (or subtract) a constant from each data point in a set, the variance of the set does not change. Thus, the variance of the elements in set A remains 12 even after subtracting 3 from each element, and the variance of the elements in set B remains 20 even after adding 2 to each element. Now, when combining variances from two datasets into one : Variance of C = n 1 × Variance of A + n 1 × ( Mean of modified A − Mean of C ) 2 + n 2 × Variance of B + n 2 × ( Mean of modified B − Mean of C ) 2 n 1 + n 2 Given : n 1 = n 2 = 5 Variance of A = 12 , Variance of B = 20 Mean of modified A = 2 , Mean of modified B = 10 , Mean of C = 6 Plugging in the values, we get : Variance of C = 5 × 12 + 5 × ( 2 − 6 ) 2 + 5 × 20 + 5 × ( 10 − 6 ) 2 10 Variance of C = 60 + 80 + 100 + 80 10 = 320 10 = 32 Step 3 : Sum of the mean and variance of set C Sum = Mean of C + Variance of C = 6 + 32 = 38 So, the correct answer is : Option C : 38.",
