    "questionEn": "An air bubble of volume 1 cm 3 rises from the bottom of a lake 40 m deep to the surface at a temperature of 12 ∘ C . The atmospheric pressure is 1 × 10 5 Pa the density of water is 1000 kg / m 3 and g = 10 m / s 2 . There is no difference of the temperature of water at the depth of 40 m and on the surface. The volume of air bubble when it reaches the surface will be:",
