    "explanationEn": "We know that, equation for SHM along x-axis is given by x = A sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ ) Let mean position for 1st particle is at x = 0 So, the SHM equation for 1st particle, x 1 = A sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 1 ) Now, as the separation between mean positions of both the particle is x 0 So, mean position for 2nd particle is x = x 0 Hence, the SHM equation for 2nd particle, x 2 = x 0 + A sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 2 ) Now, the separation between particles would be | x 2 − x 1 | = x 0 + A sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 2 ) − A sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 1 ) = x 0 + A [ sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 2 ) − sin ⁡ ( ω t + φ 1 ) ] We know, sin ⁡ C − sin ⁡ D = 2 cos ⁡ ( C + D 2 ) sin ⁡ ( C − D 2 ) Hence, | x 2 − x 1 | = x 0 + 2 A cos ⁡ ( ω t + φ 1 + φ 2 2 ) sin ⁡ ( φ 2 − φ 1 2 ) For maximum separation, Let cos ⁡ ( ω t + φ 1 + φ 2 2 ) = 1 So, | x 2 − x 1 | = x 0 + 2 A sin ⁡ ( φ 2 − φ 1 2 ) Since, | x 2 − x 1 | = x 0 + A (given) So, x 0 + A = x 0 + 2 A sin ⁡ ( φ 2 − φ 1 2 ) ⇒ sin ⁡ ( φ 2 − φ 1 2 ) = 1 2 ⇒ φ 2 − φ 1 2 = π 6 ⇒ φ 2 − φ 1 = π 3",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
