    "correctOptionIndex": 1,
    "explanationEn": "Statement - 1 : When light reflects from the air-glass plate interface, the reflected wave suffers a phase change of π. This statement is true. According to the physics of wave optics, when light reflects from a denser medium (glass in this case) to a rarer medium (air), there is a phase change of π (or 180 degrees). Statement - 2 : The center of the interference pattern is dark. This statement is also true. When a thin air film is formed between a convex lens and a plane surface, the path difference at the center of the pattern is zero. However, due to the phase change of π at the lower surface (glass surface), the two interfering waves are out of phase at the center, resulting in destructive interference and creating a dark spot at the center. So both statements are true. However, statement - 2 is not a direct explanation of statement - 1. Statement - 2 arises because of the combination of the path difference and the phase change mentioned in statement - 1, but it doesn&#39;t directly explain why the phase change occurs. Hence, the answer is : Option B : Statement - 1 is true, Statement - 2 is true, Statement - 2 is not the correct explanation of Statement - 1.",
