    "questionEn": "Let S = {1, 2, . . . . . ., 20}. A subset B of S is said to be \"nice\", if the sum of the elements of B is 203. Then the probability that a randomly chosen subset of S is \"nice\" is :",
    "optionsEn": [
      "Option A",
      "Option B",
      "Option C",
      "Option D"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "We can solve this problem by counting the number of \"nice\" subsets in the set S = {1, 2, , 20 }, and then dividing that number by the total number of possible subsets of S. The sum of all elements in S is : 1 + 2 + + 20 = = 210 Since a \"nice\" subset must sum to 203, the elements not in the subset must sum to 210 - 203 = 7. Now we need to find the ways to make the sum of 7 using the elements of S. The combinations are : 1. 7 2. 1 + 6 3. 2 + 5 4. 3 + 4 5. 1 + 2 + 4 6. 1 + 3 + 3(This doesn't work since 3 is repeated) 7. 2 + 2 + 3(This doesn't work since 2 is repeated) So, there are 5 \"nice\" subsets. Since the set S has 20 elements, there are possible subsets (including the empty set and the set itself). The probability of randomly choosing a \"nice\" subset is therefore :",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "tags": [
      "Mathematics",
      "JEE Main 2019",
      "January Session"
    ]
