    "subject": "Mathematics",
    "questionEn": "A number is called a palindrome if it reads the same backward as well as forward. For example 285582 is a six digit palindrome. The number of six digit palindromes, which are divisible by 55, is ____________.",
    "optionsEn": [
      "Option A",
      "Option B",
      "Option C",
      "Option D"
    ],
    "correctOptionIndex": 0,
    "explanationEn": "5 | a | b | b | a | 5 | For divisible by 55 it shall be divisible by 11 and 5 both, for divisibility by 5 unit digit shall be 0 or 5 but as the number is six digit palindrome unit digit is 5. A number is divisible by 11 if the difference between sum of the digits in the odd places and the sum of the digits in the even places is a multiple of 11 or zero. Sum of the digits in the even place = a + b + 5 Sum of the digits in the odd places = a + b + 5 Difference between the two sums = (a + b + 5 ) - (a + b + 5) = 0 0 is divisible by 11. Hence, 5abba5 is divisible by 11. So, required number = 10 10 = 100",
    "difficulty": "Medium",
    "tags": [
      "Mathematics",
      "JEE Main 2021",
      "August/September Session"
    ]
